    <!-- Case Study & Educational Breakdown Section -->
    <section id="explain-section" class="bg-slate-950 border-t border-slate-800 py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mt-12">
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto space-y-8">
            
            <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                <span class="text-xs bg-indigo-600/10 text-indigo-400 border border-indigo-500/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
                    Conflict Resolution Analysis
                </span>
                <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-4">Case Study: Solving the Siloed Hospital Booking System</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
                    Examine the structural breakdown of why our hospital system app failed, how we diagnosed it, and how tool integration secures direct value for patients and stakeholders alike.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Resolution Matrix Grid -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                <!-- Column 1: Conflict Type Identification -->
                <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl space-y-3">
                    <div class="text-indigo-400 text-2xl"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i></div>
                    <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">1. Conflict Type: Process & Communication</h4>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                        This scenario represents a classic <strong>Process & Communication Conflict</strong> caused by isolated workspace environments:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                        <li><strong>Designers</strong> update key requirements (WCAG contrast parameters, input sizes) inside Confluence guidelines.</li>
                        <li><strong>Developers</strong> read fixed requirements on isolated Jira cards without tracking real-time layout updates.</li>
                        <li><strong>The Result:</strong> Product components are built with compliance leaks, missing validations, and design regressions.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <!-- Column 2: Explanation of Integration -->
                <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl space-y-3">
                    <div class="text-emerald-400 text-2xl"><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate"></i></div>
                    <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">2. Jira + Confluence Synergy</h4>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                        Using Atlassian's bidirectional integration links turns static text documents into live status portals:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                        <li><strong>Bidirectional Links:</strong> Linking a Jira Issue directly displays dynamic Confluence requirement widgets in the developer panel.</li>
                        <li><strong>Dynamic Status Tags:</strong> The Confluence page lists Jira development ticket status badges, informing designers instantly when a story starts development.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <!-- Column 3: Two Conflict Resolution Steps -->
                <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl space-y-3">
                    <div class="text-blue-400 text-2xl"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i></div>
                    <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">3. Resolution Steps</h4>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                        Two crucial process changes to immediately scale development standards and stop fingers-pointing:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                        <li><strong>Step A - Definition of Ready Policy:</strong> Enforce workspace rules that stop any task from entering active sprint queues without active, verified Confluence links.</li>
                        <li><strong>Step B - Cross-Functional Alignment:</strong> Establish joint backlog grooming meetings before every single sprint.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Workflow Visual Representation -->
            <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl">
                <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-4 flex items-center">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project text-indigo-400 mr-2"></i> Agile Handoff Task-Document Link Roadmap
                </h4>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
                    <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
                        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-teal-400 uppercase">Phase 1: Concept specs</span>
                        <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-white mt-1">Confluence PRD</h5>
                        <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">Designers map requirements, user paths, and wireframes.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-xl border border-indigo-600/20 relative">
                        <div class="absolute -right-3 top-4 text-slate-700 hidden md:block"><i class="fa-solid fa-link text-xs"></i></div>
                        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-indigo-400 uppercase">Phase 2: Sync Match</span>
                        <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-white mt-1">Jira Epics Generated</h5>
                        <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">Bidirectional link establishes exact requirement values to task queues.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 relative">
                        <div class="absolute -right-3 top-4 text-slate-700 hidden md:block"><i class="fa-solid fa-link text-xs"></i></div>
                        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-blue-400 uppercase">Phase 3: Execution</span>
                        <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-white mt-1">Sprint Code Build</h5>
                        <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">Developers build app components referencing live linked design guidelines.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
                        <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase">Phase 4: Output</span>
                        <h5 class="text-xs font-semibold text-white mt-1">Verified App UI</h5>
                        <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 mt-1">Secure, accessible patient appointment bookings for public use.</p>
                    </div>
